        answer: "### English Model Answer\n1. Differences between KYC & Enhanced CDD:\n\nBasis of Comparison  |  Standard KYC / Customer Due Diligence (CDD)  |  Enhanced Customer Due Diligence (ECDD)\n\n**Applicability**  |  All standard, low to medium risk retail and corporate clients.  |  High-risk clients, Politically Exposed Persons (PEPs), casinos, and cross-border entities.\n\n**Depth of Information**  |  Basic identity proof: citizenship, address verification, photo, standard occupation.  |  Deep verification: Source of Wealth, Source of Funds, and ultimate Beneficial Ownership (UBO).\n\n**Approval Authority**  |  Branch Customer Relationship Officer / Operations Manager.  |  Mandatory prior written approval from Senior Executive Management / Chief Compliance Officer.\n\n**Surveillance Frequency**  |  Updated periodically every 2 to 3 years.  |  Continuous, real-time transaction screening and annual reviews.\n\n2. Imperative of Identifying High-Risk Customers:\nCriminals leverage high-value entities to launder proceeds of corruption and crime. Robust ECDD insulates banks from catastrophic financial penalties, regulatory sanctions, and international FATF grey-listing.\n\n***Conclusion:*** A risk-based approach ensures proportionate compliance resources are deployed against genuine illicit financing threats.\n\n### नेपाली नमूना उत्तर (Nepali Model Answer)\n१. KYC र Enhanced CDD बीचको भिन्नता (Difference between KYC & Enhanced CDD):\n\nतुलनाको आधार (Basis)  |  साधारण ग्राहक पहिचान (Standard KYC / CDD)  |  विस्तृत ग्राहक पहिचान (Enhanced CDD - ECDD)\n\n**लागु हुने वर्ग**  |  सबै सामान्य तथा न्यून/मध्यम जोखिम भएका ग्राहकहरूका लागि।  |  उच्च जोखिम (High-Risk) भएका व्यक्ति, PEPs र जटिल संस्थाहरूका लागि।\n\n**सूचनाको गहिराइ**  |  नाम, ठेगाना, नागरिकता, फोटो र सामान्य पेसा/व्यवसायको जानकारी।  |  सम्पत्तिको वास्तविक स्रोत (Source of Wealth), कोषको स्रोत (Source of Funds), र वास्तविक लाभग्राही (Beneficial Owner) को गहिरो प्रमाणीकरण।\n\n**स्वीकृति तह**  |  शाखाको ग्राहक 