        questionTextNepali: "Process र Thread बीच भिन्नता छुट्याउनुहोस्। User-Level Threads (ULT) र Kernel-Level Threads (KLT) व्याख्या गर्नुहोस्।",
        options: null,
        marks: 5,
        marksBreakdown: "5",
        answer: "### English Model Answer\n1. Process vs Thread: A process is an independent program in execution with its own private address space, PCB, and system resources. A thread is a lightweight execution unit within a process sharing the same address space, code, and data sections, but maintaining its own stack, registers, and program counter.\n2. ULT vs KLT:\n• User-Level Threads (ULT): Managed by thread libraries in user space without kernel awareness. Fast context switching without system calls, but if one thread blocks on I/O, the entire process is blocked.\n• Kernel-Level Threads (KLT): Managed directly by the OS kernel scheduler. True multi-core parallel execution; if one thread blocks, other threads continue running, though context switches incur kernel transitions.\n\n### नेपाली नमूना उत्तर (Nepali Model Answer)\n१. Process र Thread: प्रोसेस भन्नाले आफ्नै निजी मेमोरी र स्रोत भएको स्वतन्त्र प्रोग्रामलाई बुझाउँछ। थ्रेड भन्नाले एउटै प्रोसेसभित्र रहने सानो कार्य एकाइ हो जसले प्रोसेसको साझा मेमोरी प्रयोग गर्दछ।\n२. ULT र KLT:\n• User-Level Threads: युजर स्पेसको लाइब्रेरीमार्फत व्यवस्थापन हुने, छिटो चल्ने तर एउटा थ्रेड रोकिँदा पूरै प्रोसेस रोकिन सक्ने।\n• Kernel-Level Threads: सिधै अपरेटिङ सिस्टमको कर्नेलद्वारा व्यवस्थापन हुने, मल्टिकोर प्रोसेसरमा वास्तविक रूपमा समानान्तर चल्न सक्ने।",
