        questionText: "Explain Inter-Process Communication (IPC). Compare Shared Memory and Message Passing mechanisms in operating systems.",
        questionTextNepali: "Inter-Process Communication (IPC) व्याख्या गर्नुहोस्। Shared Memory र Message Passing संयन्त्रहरू बीच तुलना गर्नुहोस्।",
        options: null,
        marks: 5,
        marksBreakdown: "5",
        answer: "### English Model Answer\n1. IPC Overview: Mechanisms enabling cooperating processes to exchange data, synchronize actions, and coordinate execution.\n2. Comparison:\n• Shared Memory: Processes map a common physical memory region into their virtual address spaces. Communication occurs at memory bus speeds with zero kernel intervention after initial setup. Requires explicit synchronization mechanisms (Semaphores, Mutex) to prevent race conditions.\n• Message Passing: Processes communicate by exchanging explicit messages through kernel primitives (`send()` and `receive()`). Slower due to kernel context switches and buffer copying, but ideal for distributed or multi-server environments without shared memory.\n\n### नेपाली नमूना उत्तर (Nepali Model Answer)\n१. IPC को अवधारणा: अपरेटिङ सिस्टममा चलिरहेका विभिन्न प्रोसेसहरू बीच डाटा आदानप्रदान र समन्वय गर्ने विधिलाई IPC भनिन्छ।\n२. तुलना:\n• Shared Memory: दुई वा बढी प्रोसेसहरूले साझा मेमोरी प्रयोग गरेर डाटा साट्छन्। यो अत्यन्त छिटो हुन्छ तर रेस कन्डिसन रोक्न सेमाफोर आवश्यक पर्छ।\n• Message Passing: कर्नेलको सहायताले सन्देश पठाएर (Send/Receive) कुराकानी गरिन्छ। यो अलि सुस्त भए पनि फरक-फरक कम्प्युटर बीच काम गर्न उपयुक्त हुन्छ।",
