        answer: "### English Model Answer\n1. Banker's Algorithm Overview: A deadlock avoidance algorithm developed by Edsger Dijkstra that tests for safety by simulating the allocation of predetermined maximum possible amounts of resources before granting requests.\n2. Data Structures: Available Vector, Max Matrix, Allocation Matrix, and Need Matrix (`Need[i][j] = Max[i][j] - Allocation[i][j]`).\n3. Safe vs Unsafe State:\n• Safe State: There exists at least one sequence of processes <P1, P2, ..., Pn> such that for each Pi, the resources that Pi can still request can be satisfied by currently available resources plus resources held by all preceding processes. Deadlock is mathematically impossible.\n• Unsafe State: No guaranteed safe execution sequence exists. While an unsafe state is not automatically a deadlock, it can lead to deadlock if processes request their maximum claims.\n\n### नेपाली नमूना उत्तर (Nepali Model Answer)\n१. ब्याङ्कर्स एल्गोरिदम: कुनै प्रोसेसले स्रोत माग्दा उक्त स्रोत दिँदा प्रणाली सुरक्षित रहन्छ कि रहँदैन भनी जाँच गरेर मात्र स्रोत बाँड्ने विधि।\n२. आवश्यक विवरणहरू: उपलब्ध स्रोत (Available), अधिकतम माग (Max), दिइसकिएको स्रोत (Allocation), र बाँकी आवश्यक स्रोत (Need)।\n३. Safe र Unsafe State:\n• Safe State: प्रणालीसँग कम्तीमा यस्तो एउटा क्रम उपलब्ध हुन्छ जसबाट सबै प्रोसेसहरूले पालो अनुसार स्रोत पाएर आफ्नो काम सुरक्षित रूपमा सम्पन्न गर्न सक्छन्।\n• Unsafe State: कुनै पनि सुरक्षित क्रम नभएको अवस्था। यसमा डेडलोक हुन सक्ने उच्च जोखिम हुन्छ।",
