      ModelQuestion(
        number: 5,
        questionText: "Explain Page Replacement Algorithms: FIFO, Least Recently Used (LRU), and Optimal (OPT). What is Belady's Anomaly?",
        questionTextNepali: "पेज रिप्लेसमेन्ट एल्गोरिदमहरू (FIFO, LRU, Optimal) व्याख्या गर्नुहोस्। Belady's Anomaly के हो?",
        options: null,
        marks: 5,
        marksBreakdown: "5",
        answer: "### English Model Answer\n1. Page Replacement: Invoked during a Page Fault when all physical frames are occupied and a victim frame must be evicted.\n2. Algorithms:\n• First-In, First-Out (FIFO): Evicts the oldest page brought into memory. Simple to implement with a queue.\n• Least Recently Used (LRU): Evicts the page that has not been referenced for the longest period of time. Approximates optimal replacement using timestamp or stack.\n• Optimal (OPT): Evicts the page that will not be used for the longest period of time in the future. Theoretical benchmark; impossible to implement in practice.\n3. Belady's Anomaly: A phenomenon in FIFO where increasing the number of physical frames paradoxically increases the number of page faults.\n\n### नेपाली नमूना उत्तर (Nepali Model Answer)\n१. पेज रिप्लेसमेन्ट: जब मेमोरी भरिन्छ र नयाँ पेज ल्याउनुपर्छ, कुन पुरानो पेजलाई बाहिर निकाल्ने भनी छनोट गर्ने विधि।\n२. एल्गोरिदमहरू:\n• FIFO: सबैभन्दा पहिले आएको पेजलाई पहिले हटाउने।\n• LRU: लामो समयदेखि प्रयोग नभएको पेजलाई हटाउने। यो धेरै प्रभावकारी हुन्छ।\n• Optimal: भविष्यमा सबैभन्दा पछि प्रयोग हुने पेज हटाउने (सैद्धान्तिक मात्र)।\n३. Belady's Anomaly: FIFO मा धेरै मेमोरी फ्रेम थप्दा पनि उल्टै पेज फल्ट बढ्ने अनौठो समस्या।",
