        questionText: "Explain DMA (Direct Memory Access) transfer modes: Burst Mode, Cycle Stealing Mode, and Transparent Mode. What are the advantages of DMA in database servers?",
        questionTextNepali: "DMA का डाटा ट्रान्सफर मोडहरू (Burst, Cycle Stealing, Transparent Mode) व्याख्या गर्नुहोस्। डाटाबेस सर्भरमा DMA को फाइदा के छ?",
        options: null,
        marks: 5,
        marksBreakdown: "5",
        answer: "### English Model Answer\n1. Direct Memory Access (DMA): Allows high-speed I/O peripherals to transfer blocks directly to/from RAM without CPU intervention.\n\n2. Transfer Modes:\n• Burst Mode: DMA controller takes complete control of system bus, transferring an entire data block continuously. CPU is paused during transfer.\n• Cycle Stealing Mode: DMA controller takes control of system bus for only one bus cycle at a time between CPU cycles. Minimizes CPU stalling.\n• Transparent Mode: DMA controller transfers data only when CPU executes internal operations without utilizing the system bus.\n\n3. Database Server Benefits: Transfers multi-gigabyte transaction logs and table partitions between NVMe arrays and RAM at bus speed while CPU cores focus exclusively on SQL execution.\n\n### नेपाली नमूना उत्तर (Nepali Model Answer)\n१. Direct Memory Access: CPU लाई संलग्न नगराई बाह्य उपकरण र मुख्य मेमोरी बीच सिधै डाटा आदानप्रदान गर्ने प्रविधि।\n\n२. ट्रान्सफर मोडहरू:\n• Burst Mode: सम्पूर्ण डाटा नसकिउन्जेल बसमा पूर्ण नियन्त्रण राख्छ।\n• Cycle Stealing Mode: CPU को दुई चक्रको बीचमा एक-एक साइकल मात्र बस प्रयोग गर्छ।\n• Transparent Mode: CPU ले बस प्रयोग नगरेको समयमा मात्र डाटा सार्दछ।\n\n३. डाटाबेस सर्भरमा फाइदा: ठूला डाटाबेस लग र टेबलहरू सिधै मेमोरीमा लोड गर्न सकिन्छ, जसले गर्दा CPU गणना कार्यमा व्यस्त रहन पाउँछ।",
