        options: null,
        marks: 5,
        marksBreakdown: "5",
        answer: "### English Model Answer\n1. Database Indexing: Auxiliary data structures providing O(log N) lookup instead of costly O(N) full table scans.\n2. B-Tree vs B+ Tree:\n• B-Tree: Keys and actual record data pointers are stored in both internal nodes and leaf nodes. Search can terminate early at internal node.\n• B+ Tree: Internal nodes store only indexing search keys; all data records reside strictly in leaf nodes. Leaf nodes are linked via a bidirectional linked list.\n3. Why B+ Tree is Preferred in RDBMS: Range queries (`WHERE date BETWEEN x AND y`) are ultra-fast in B+ Trees because the engine simply scans the linked leaf nodes sequentially without traversing tree roots repeatedly.\n\n### नेपाली नमूना उत्तर (Nepali Model Answer)\n१. डाटाबेस इन्डेक्सिङको अवधारणा: पुस्तकको अन्त्यमा रहेको अनुक्रमणिका जस्तै, पूरै डाटाबेस नखोजी सिधै खोजेको रेकर्ड तुरुन्तै पत्ता लगाउने प्रविधि।\n२. B-Tree र B+ Tree को तुलना:\n• B-Tree: मुख्य डाटाका पोइन्टरहरू रूखका बीचका हाँगा र पात दुवैमा हुन्छन्।\n• B+ Tree: बीचका हाँगाहरूमा की (Key) मात्र हुन्छन् र वास्तविक डाटा सबैभन्दा तल्लो तह (पात) मा मात्र हुन्छ। सबै पातहरू एकआपसमा जोडिएका हुन्छन्।\n३. बैंकिङमा फाइदा: मिति वा रकमको दायरा (Range Query) खोज्न B+ Tree अत्यन्त छिटो हुन्छ।",
