        questionTextNepali: "IPSec VPN आर्किटेक्चर व्याख्या गर्नुहोस्। AH र ESP, तथा Transport Mode र Tunnel Mode बीच भिन्नता छुट्याउनुहोस्।",
        options: null,
        marks: 5,
        marksBreakdown: "5",
        answer: "### English Model Answer\n1. IPSec Architecture: Suite of protocols operating at OSI Network Layer to secure IP communications between branch offices and data centers.\n\n2. Security Protocols:\n• Authentication Header (AH): Provides data integrity and origin authentication, but NO encryption (plaintext payload).\n• Encapsulating Security Payload (ESP): Provides encryption (confidentiality), data integrity, and anti-replay protection. Industry standard for banking VPNs.\n\n3. Operational Modes:\n• Transport Mode: Encrypts only payload; original IP header remains unencrypted. Used for host-to-host communication.\n• Tunnel Mode: Encrypts entire original packet (header + payload) and prepends a brand-new outer IP header. Used for site-to-site branch router connections.\n\n### नेपाली नमूना उत्तर (Nepali Model Answer)\n१. IPSec VPN को अवधारणा: बैंकका शाखाहरू र केन्द्रीय डाटा सेन्टर बीच इन्टरनेटमार्फत सुरक्षित सुरुङ (Tunnel) बनाएर डाटा पठाउने प्रविधि।\n\n२. सुरक्षा प्रोटोकलहरू: AH (अखण्डता र प्रामाणिकता दिन्छ तर इन्क्रिप्सन गर्दैन) र ESP (डाटालाई पूर्ण इन्क्रिप्ट र सुरक्षित गर्दछ)।\n\n३. मोडहरू: Transport Mode (कम्प्युटर-कम्प्युटर बीच) र Tunnel Mode (शाखा-शाखा बीचको नेटवर्कमा पूरै प्याकेट इन्क्रिप्ट हुने)।",
