      ModelQuestion(
        number: 6,
        questionText: "Explain Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA). Differentiate between SMS OTP, Time-Based OTP (TOTP), and FIDO2 / WebAuthn Hardware Keys.",
        questionTextNepali: "Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA) व्याख्या गर्नुहोस्। SMS OTP, Time-Based OTP (TOTP) र FIDO2 हार्डवेयर की बीच तुलना गर्नुहोस्।",
        options: null,
        marks: 5,
        marksBreakdown: "5",
        answer: "### English Model Answer\n1. MFA Concept: Requires two or more independent authentication factors: Something you know (password), Something you have (OTP token/device), Something you are (biometrics).\n2. Comparison:\n• SMS OTP: Transmitted over cellular SS7 channels. Highly vulnerable to SIM-Swapping, SS7 interception, and phishing proxies. Lowest security.\n• Time-Based One-Time Password (TOTP): Cryptographically generated on authenticator app (Google Authenticator) via HMAC of shared secret key and current timestamp. Immune to SIM swaps, but vulnerable to reverse-proxy phishing (Evilginx).\n• FIDO2 / WebAuthn: Hardware security tokens (YubiKey) utilizing public key cryptography. Browser binds origin URL cryptographically to authentication challenge, rendering credential phishing mathematically impossible.\n\n### नेपाली नमूना उत्तर (Nepali Model Answer)\n१. MFA को अवधारणा: पासवर्ड बाहेक थप सुरक्षा तह (ओटीपी, औंठाछाप) प्रयोग गरेर मात्र खाता खोल्न दिने प्रणाली।\n२. तुलना:\n• SMS OTP: मोबाइलमा म्यासेज आउने विधि। सजिलो भए पनि सिम-स्वापिङ वा टेलिकम ह्याकिङबाट चोरी हुन सक्ने जोखिम।\n• TOTP: मोबाइल एपमा प्रत्येक ३० सेकेन्डमा बदलिने कोड (Google Authenticator)। यो सुरक्षित हुन्छ।\n• FIDO2 हार्डवेयर की: USB पेनड्राइभ जस्तो सेक्युरिटी की, जसले नक्कली वेबसाइटमा कहिल्यै पासवर्ड जान दिँदैन। यो सबैभन्दा सुरक्षित प्रणाली हो।",
