      ModelQuestion(
        number: 2,
        questionText: "Explain the principle of Locality of Reference (Temporal Locality and Spatial Locality). How does it justify the effectiveness of Cache Memory?",
        questionTextNepali: "Locality of Reference (Temporal र Spatial Locality) को सिद्धान्त व्याख्या गर्नुहोस्। यसले क्यास मेमोरीको उपयोगितालाई कसरी पुष्टि गर्दछ?",
        options: null,
        marks: 5,
        marksBreakdown: "5",
        answer: "### English Model Answer\n1. Locality of Reference: Empirical observation that executing programs access a relatively small portion of their address space at any given time.\n2. Dimensions:\n• Temporal Locality (Locality in Time): If a memory location is referenced once, it is highly likely to be referenced again in the near future (e.g., loop variables, subroutine calls, transaction state variables). Cache retains recently referenced blocks.\n• Spatial Locality (Locality in Space): If a memory location is referenced, nearby memory locations are likely to be referenced soon (e.g., sequential instruction execution, array traversals). Cache fetches entire blocks/lines rather than single bytes.\n3. Cache Justification: Allows small, fast SRAM caches (1-3% of RAM capacity) to service 95%+ of memory requests.\n\n### नेपाली नमूना उत्तर (Nepali Model Answer)\n१. Locality of Reference को अवधारणा: कम्प्युटर प्रोग्राम चल्दा छोटो समयभित्र सीमित मेमोरी क्षेत्रमा पटकपटक पहुँच गर्ने प्रवृत्तिको सिद्धान्त।\n२. प्रकारहरू:\n• Temporal Locality: भर्खरै प्रयोग भएको डाटा निकट भविष्यमा फेरि प्रयोग हुने सम्भावना (जस्तै: लूप रिएबल)।\n• Spatial Locality: कुनै डाटा प्रयोग भएपछि त्यसको नजिकै रहेको डाटा पनि छिट्टै प्रयोग हुने सम्भावना (जस्तै: एरे र क्रमिक निर्देशनहरू)।\n३. क्यासको उपयोगिता: यसै सिद्धान्तका कारण सानो क्यास मेमोरी राख्दा पनि ९५% भन्दा बढी डाटा क्यासबाटै तुरुन्त प्राप्त हुन्छ।",
      ),
      ModelQuestion(
        number: 3,
        questionText: "Explain Bus Arbitration in computer architecture. Compare Centralized Arbitration (Daisy Chaining, Polling) with Distributed Arbitration.",
        questionTextNepali: "कम्प्युटर आर्किटेक्चरमा Bus Arbitration व्याख्या गर्नुहोस्। Centralized र Distributed Arbitration बीच तुलना गर्नुहोस्।",
        options: null,
        marks: 5,
        marksBreakdown: "5",
        answer: "### English Model Answer\n1. Bus Arbitration: The mechanism by which multiple bus masters (CPU cores, DMA controllers) coordinate ownership of shared system address and data buses.\n2. Schemes:\n• Daisy Chaining (Centralized): Bus Grant signal propagates serially through all master devices. Highest priority closest to arbiter; lowest priority prone to starvation.\n• Polling (Centralized): Bus controller steps through master device IDs on polling lines. Flexible priority sequencing.\n• Independent Request (Centralized): Each master has dedicated Bus Request and Bus Grant lines to arbiter. Fast, but higher pin count.\n• Distributed Arbitration: Devices determine priority collaboratively using unique priority codes on shared lines without single point of failure.\n\n### नेपाली नमूना उत्तर (Nepali Model Answer)\n१. Bus Arbitration को अवधारणा: जब एकभन्दा बढी उपकरणहरूले एकै पटक साझा कम्प्युटर बस प्रयोग गर्न खोज्छन्, कसलाई पहिले प्रयोग गर्न दिने भनी निर्णय गर्ने विधि।\n२. विधिहरू:\n• Daisy Chaining: सिरियल तारमार्फत पालैपालो अनुमति दिने। नजिकको उपकरणले बढी प्राथमिकता पाउँछ।\n• Polling: कन्ट्रोलरले पालैपालो सबै डिभाइसलाई सोध्ने।\n• Distributed: कुनै केन्द्रीय कन्ट्रोलर बिना सबै डिभाइसहरूले आपसमा मिलेर प्राथमिकता निर्धारण गर्ने।",
      ),
      ModelQuestion(
