        questionText: "Explain Network Address Translation (NAT): Static NAT, Dynamic NAT, and Port Address Translation (PAT). How does PAT conserve public IPv4 addresses?",
        questionTextNepali: "Network Address Translation (NAT) व्याख्या गर्नुहोस्: Static, Dynamic र PAT। PAT ले पब्लिक IPv4 ठेगाना कसरी बचत गर्छ?",
        options: null,
        marks: 5,
        marksBreakdown: "5",
        answer: "### English Model Answer\n1. NAT Concept: Modifies network address information in IP packet headers while in transit across an edge router.\n2. Types:\n• Static NAT: One-to-one permanent mapping of an internal private IP to a designated public IP. Used for public-facing bank servers.\n• Dynamic NAT: Maps private IPs to a pool of available public IPs on first-come, first-served basis.\n• Port Address Translation (PAT / NAT Overload): Maps thousands of internal private IP addresses to a SINGLE public IP address by tracking unique Layer 4 source port numbers.\n3. Conservation: Allows an entire commercial bank branch with 500+ workstations to share a single public IPv4 address simultaneously.\n\n### नेपाली नमूना उत्तर (Nepali Model Answer)\n१. NAT को अवधारणा: बैंकको आन्तरिक निजी (Private) IP लाई इन्टरनेटमा चल्ने सार्वजनिक (Public) IP मा बदल्ने प्रविधि।\n२. प्रकारहरू:\n• Static NAT: एउटा प्राइभेट IP का लागि एउटा स्थायी पब्लिक IP।\n• Dynamic NAT: उपलब्ध पब्लिक IP को समूहबाट पालैपालो बाँड्ने।\n• Port Address Translation (PAT): एउटै पब्लिक IP र फरक-फरक पोर्ट नम्बर प्रयोग गरेर सयौं कम्प्युटरहरूलाई इन्टरनेट चलाउन दिने। यसले सीमित IPv4 ठेगानाको अत्यधिक बचत गर्छ।",
